<title>USA: Monterey Bay Bancorp Inc Q4 shr rises.</title>
<headline>Monterey Bay Bancorp Inc Q4 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>WATSONVILLE, Calif. 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter Ended December 31,</p>
<p>						    1996		 1995</p>
<p> Interest income			     $6,689	    $5,889</p>
<p> Interest expense			     4,005	     3,694</p>
<p>Net interest income before</p>
<p>  provision for loan losses		 2,684	     2,195</p>
<p> Provision for loan losses			6		 473</p>
<p>Net interest income after</p>
<p>  provision for loan losses		 2,678	     1,722</p>
<p> Total noninterest income		     306		 238</p>
<p> General and administrative expense     2,118	     1,850</p>
<p> Income before income taxes		   866		 110</p>
<p> Income tax					 363		  30</p>
<p> Net income					 503		  80</p>
<p> Earnings per share			    0.16		0.03</p>
<p>				     Twelve Months Ended December 31,</p>
<p>						    1996		 1995</p>
<p> Interest income			    $23,986	   $22,544</p>
<p> Interest expense			    14,333	    14,227</p>
<p>Net interest income before</p>
<p>  provision for loan losses		 9,653	     8,317</p>
<p> Provision for loan losses		     28		 663</p>
<p>Net interest income after</p>
<p>  provision for loan losses		 9,625	     7,654</p>
<p> Total noninterest income		     941		 573</p>
<p>General and administrative expense (a)</p>
<p>						    9,091	     7,140</p>
<p> Earnings before income taxes	     1,475	     1,087</p>
<p> Income tax					 623		 414</p>
<p> Net income					 852		 673</p>
<p> Earnings per share (b)			0.27		0.17</p>
<p> Average rate earned on earning assets  7.46%	     7.20%</p>
<p>Average rate paid on interest</p>
<p>  bearing liabilities			 5.07%	     5.22%</p>
<p> Interest rate spread			 2.39%	     1.98%</p>
<p> Net interest margin			  3.00%	     2.65%</p>
<p>NOTES: (a) General and administrative expenses for 1996 includes a non-recurring special insurance premium assessment of $1.387 million recorded in Q3.</p>
<p>(b) 1995 EPS based on net income from February 14, 1995, the date Monterey Bay Bank (formerly Watsonville Federal Savings and Loan Association) converted to a federally chartered stock association and Monterey Bay Bancorp Inc became the holding company for the Association.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
